@lang en
IMPORT `msig-cgl-tests-fixtures`

-- THE HOSTILE READING: evidence for the findings in NOTES.md §4, one section per finding
-- the encoding can demonstrate. Each assertion states what the policy, as encoded, answers
-- in a scenario a policyholder or the insurer would care about. They PASS: a finding is a
-- defect in the instrument, shown by the encoding answering as the text makes it answer.
-- Findings that are reading only have no section here.

§ `Findings`

§§ `X1 — the claims-made trigger stacked on occurrence-dated definitions (src:59, 164, 731-736)`

-- The P&CO part needs the harm to OCCUR in the period (definitions) AND the claim to be
-- MADE in the period (Claims Made Basis 1). Harm on 31 December 2026, claim on 1 January
-- 2027: outside this policy for the claim, and outside a 2027 renewal for the harm.
`a 2027 renewal` MEANS
    `The policy as declared` WITH
        `coverage parts identified in the declarations`          IS `both parts`
        `the named insured is designated in the declarations as` IS `an organization`
        `the policy period begins`                               IS YMD 2027 1 1
        `the policy period ends`                                 IS YMD 2027 12 31
        `the retroactive date stated in the policy schedule`     IS JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)
        `the limits stated in the schedule`                      IS `a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion`
`a product injury on 31 December 2026, claimed on 1 January 2027` MEANS
    `a claim against` `the named insured` `for` `bodily injury` `on` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, claimed on` (JUST (YMD 2027 1 1)) `, where` `the products facts`
#ASSERT `the answer under the P&CO Coverage Part` `the policy` `a product injury on 31 December 2026, claimed on 1 January 2027` EQUALS `not covered` `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the claim was not made during the policy period`
#ASSERT `the answer under the P&CO Coverage Part` `a 2027 renewal` `a product injury on 31 December 2026, claimed on 1 January 2027` EQUALS `not covered` `I: the harm did not occur during the policy period`
-- And the Retroactive Date (1 January 2020) buys nothing: an injury in 2025, after it,
-- claimed in 2026, fails the definition of bodily injury.
#ASSERT `the answer under the P&CO Coverage Part` `the policy` (`a claim against` `the named insured` `for` `bodily injury` `on` (YMD 2025 11 1) `, claimed on` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) `, where` `the products facts`) EQUALS `not covered` `I: the harm did not occur during the policy period`

§§ `X2 — "anywhere in the world" for products, cut back to suits brought in Vietnam (src:153-157, 46-49)`

-- A product sold for use in Vietnam injures a buyer abroad, who sues where injured.
`a buyer injured abroad who sues there` MEANS
    `a products claim where` (LIST `it is not the case that` `the harm occurs within a nation or area described in the Policy`,
                                   `it is the case that` `the damages arise out of a product sold for use or consumption within the territory described in the Policy`,
                                   `it is the case that` `a suit for the damages has been brought`)
#ASSERT `P&CO:` `a buyer injured abroad who sues there` EQUALS `not covered` `IV: the harm did not occur within the policy territory`
#ASSERT `the harm occurs in a place the policy territory names` `a buyer injured abroad who sues there`

§§ `X3 — the CGL part's products and completed operations aggregates have nothing to apply to (src:512-514, 535-536, 710-713)`

#ASSERT `CGL III Coverage A — the occurrence falls under the bodily injury aggregate` `the ordinary products claim`
#ASSERT `CGL:` `the ordinary products claim` EQUALS `not covered` `COMPLETED OPERATIONS HAZARD AND PRODUCTS HAZARD EXCLUSION CLAUSE`

§§ `X4 — the two caps in two foreign currencies (src:28, 34, 942, 949)`

-- Same sums, same hypothetical rates: 90,550,000 under the clause as printed with US
-- dollar caps, 89,100,000 under the Ultimate Net Loss Clause with Singapore dollar caps.
#ASSERT `the Supplementary Payments, as printed with US dollar caps` `the ordinary sums` `the hypothetical rates` EQUALS 90_550_000
#ASSERT (`the ultimate net loss of` `the ordinary sums` `at` `the hypothetical rates` MINUS `Ultimate Net Loss 2(a)` `the ordinary sums`) EQUALS 89_100_000

§§ `X5 — separate limits do not say which limit absorbs defence and the other sums (src:18, 504-540)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the most the Company pays for the occurrence under` `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part` `, for` `a policy with separate limits` `,` `the ordinary CGL claim` `,` (`the ordinary sums, with damages of` 1_000_000_000 `for bodily injury and` 500_000_000 `for property damage`) `,` `the hypothetical rates` `,` `nothing paid yet` BECAUSE "the Policy does not say which limit absorbs the other sums when one occurrence causes both bodily injury and property damage"

§§ `X6 — "did not know or could not reasonably have foreseen" (src:734-736)`

-- No insured knew, but it could reasonably have been foreseen: the proviso as written
-- holds; the reading an insurer would argue for does not.
`foreseeable but not known` MEANS `a products claim where` (`only` `at the effective date of the policy an insured could reasonably have foreseen that the harm might be expected to be the basis of a claim or suit`)
#ASSERT `Claims Made Basis 1 — the proviso on knowledge at the effective date holds` `foreseeable but not known`
#ASSERT NOT `Claims Made Basis 1 — the proviso on knowledge, read as "neither knew nor could have foreseen"` `foreseeable but not known`

§§ `X7 — notice of circumstances saves a later products claim, not a completed operations claim (src:746-750)`

GIVEN facts IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a 2027 claim, circumstances notified in November 2026, where` facts MEANS
    `A claim against an insured` WITH
        `the person claimed against`                                      IS `the named insured`
        `the harm`                                                        IS `bodily injury, sickness or disease sustained by a person`
        `the date the injury occurs`                                      IS YMD 2026 11 1
        `the date of the occurrence`                                      IS YMD 2026 11 1
        `the occurrence`                                                  IS "the occurrence"
        `the general conditions of exposure`                              IS NOTHING
        `the date the claim was first made in writing against an insured` IS JUST (YMD 2027 2 1)
        `the date an insured first became aware of circumstances which may give rise to the claim` IS JUST (YMD 2026 11 2)
        `the date written notice of those circumstances was given to the Company` IS JUST (YMD 2026 11 5)
        `the claim series`                                                IS NOTHING
        `the findings`                                                    IS append (`only` `the claim arises out of the named insured's products to which the notified circumstances relate`) (append facts `the ordinary findings`)
#ASSERT `P&CO:` (`a 2027 claim, circumstances notified in November 2026, where` `the products facts`) EQUALS `covered`
#ASSERT `P&CO:` (`a 2027 claim, circumstances notified in November 2026, where` `the completed operations facts`) EQUALS `not covered` `CLAIMS MADE BASIS 1: the claim was not made during the policy period`

§§ `X8 — any departure from any term bars the action (src:231-234)`

-- A judgement after trial, but notice was late (no "full compliance"): no action lies.
#ASSERT NOT `Condition 4 — an action lies against the Company` (`a bodily injury claim where` (LIST `it is not the case that` `there has been full compliance with all of the terms of the Policy`, `it is the case that` `the insured's obligation to pay has been finally determined by judgement against the insured after actual trial`))

§§ `X10 — the War and Terrorism Exclusion on the Company's say-so (src:976-977)`

-- No finding of war or terrorism at all; the Company alleges the exclusion and the
-- insured has not proved the contrary.
#ASSERT `CGL:` (`a bodily injury claim where` (`only` `the Company alleges that by reason of the War and Terrorism Exclusion the loss is not covered`)) EQUALS `not covered` `WAR AND TERRORISM EXCLUSION`

§§ `X11 — the Cyber Liability Exclusion reaches business done by e-mail (src:819-821)`

-- A product ordered and invoiced by e-mail injures its buyer.
#ASSERT `P&CO:` (`a products claim where` (`only` `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the transmission of electronic mail or documents by electronic means`)) EQUALS `not covered` `CYBER LIABILITY EXCLUSION`
#ASSERT `CGL:` (`a bodily injury claim where` (`only` `the claim or loss arises out of activities or business conducted or transacted via the Internet, an Intranet or an Extranet`)) EQUALS `not covered` `CYBER LIABILITY EXCLUSION`

§§ `X14 — defence and the other sums come out of the limit (src:18, 923-924)`

-- Damages of 4,950,000,000 plus the ordinary other sums of 89,100,000 make 5,039,100,000;
-- the Company pays its 5,000,000,000 limit, and 39,100,000 of the DAMAGES are left with
-- the insured because the defence was paid out of the same limit.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays under` `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part` `, for` `the policy` `,` `the ordinary CGL claim` `,` (`the ordinary sums, with damages of` 4_950_000_000 `for bodily injury and` 0 `for property damage`) `,` `the hypothetical rates` `,` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS 5_000_000_000

§§ `X15 — the named insured's employees are not insureds (src:462-499, 643-657)`

-- An employee sued personally for injuring a visitor while at work, on foot, not
-- operating mobile equipment: no cover for the employee under either part.
#ASSERT `CGL:` (`a claim against` `an employee of the named insured` `for` `bodily injury` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, claimed on` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) `, where` EMPTY) EQUALS `not covered` `PERSONS INSURED: the person claimed against is not an insured`

§§ `X16 — under the combined single limit the CGL part has no aggregate at all (src:808-810, 710-713)`

-- The whole 10 billion aggregate already paid out: a premises occurrence is still paid
-- in full, because the aggregate reaches only products and completed operations, which
-- the CGL part excludes. Every premises occurrence in the year gets a fresh 5 billion.
#ASSERT `what the Company pays under` `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part` `, for` `the policy` `,` `the ordinary CGL claim` `,` `the ordinary sums` `,` `the hypothetical rates` `,` (`already paid: combined` 10_000_000_000 `, bodily injury` 0 `, property damage` 0) EQUALS 1_089_100_000

§§ `X18 — the refund on the insured's own cancellation cannot be computed from the policy (src:297, 182-183)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Condition 9 — the earned premium when` `the named insured` `cancels, on a premium of` 100_000_000 `for a period from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, cancelled on` (YMD 2026 7 1) BECAUSE "Condition 9: the customary short rate table and procedure are not in the document"
